    "notes": "refundable: mixed. Line 38 is the NONREFUNDABLE general business credit and goes to Schedule 3 Part I line 6a. Part III line 6 column (j) \u2014 the net elective payment election amount \u2014 is REFUNDABLE and goes to Schedule 3 Part II line 13c, which is the route by which an elective-pay (direct pay) energy credit becomes cash. This form is the collecting point for the business-use half of two credits in this slice: Form 8936 line 8 (new clean vehicle, business/investment use) arrives at Part III line 1y, Form 8936 line 21 (qualified commercial clean vehicle) at Part III line 1aa, and Form 8911 line 3 (alternative fuel vehicle refueling property, business/investment use) at Part III line 1s. PART III IS NOW DECLARED IN FULL \u2014 all of lines 1a through 1zz, 2, 3, 4a through 4z, 5 and 6, each with its ten columns (a) through (j) \u2014 transcribed verbatim from pages 4 and 5 of the form. It was previously cut down to the three lines this slice itself feeds, and that was wrong: the Schedule K-1 routes from the pass-through part of this map land on roughly forty different Part III letters, and a line this form does not declare is a figure a leadsheet cannot fetch. Each caption is the name of the SOURCE credit form that feeds that line, which is how the form is printed. Lines 1r, 1z, 1hh, 1ii, 4l and 4m read 'Reserved' and are declared as such rather than omitted, so that a route arriving at one is recognisably arriving at a reserved line rather than at a line nobody transcribed. Printed revision: Form 3800 (2025), Created 8/19/25.",
